     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve gotten this same error using the galaxy maaslin module. I believe it occurs whenever there is any kind of problem in the metadata rows. I have encountered it by having data presented alphabetically when it expected numeric (M/F instead of 1/0 for Sex) and when I tried submitting data where I had data from the same site at two different time points. It seems like not all metadata rows will accept the same entry across multiple samples, the exceptions being sex, age, cohort, etc. Or possibly I have been trying to call the metadata row by an unaccepted name. I&#39;m still working that one out, and would love to hear if anyone ha solved this issue.<br>David <br><br>On Thursday, September 14, 2017 at 11:27:45 AM UTC-4, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">valentin...@cri-paris.org</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear MaAsLin users,<div><br></div><div>I have been trying to run MaAsLin analysis on Galaxy but am facing issues.</div><div><br></div><div>When I run my analysis, I get the following error message:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-XZQdaG55GWI/WbqUYoX_DNI/AAAAAAAAAAM/2JCq3QmT5mgooL244HGajzdUPo8J_R-7wCLcBGAs/s1600/maaslinerror.PNG\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-XZQdaG55GWI/WbqUYoX_DNI/AAAAAAAAAAM/2JCq3QmT5mgooL244HGajzdUPo8J_R-7wCLcBGAs/s1600/maaslinerror.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793235121066000&amp;usg=AOvVaw010j-RIZQyEW0ZKcXvJv7A\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-XZQdaG55GWI/WbqUYoX_DNI/AAAAAAAAAAM/2JCq3QmT5mgooL244HGajzdUPo8J_R-7wCLcBGAs/s1600/maaslinerror.PNG\" border=\"0\"></a> </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><di